# Session decks - the checks to run before a deck reaches Sathya

One screen. The house system, his edits and where they came from are in `references/rules.md` in this folder - read that once at the start of a deck, then run this list on every slide. Every line traces to a section there, named in parentheses. `writing-to-teach` governs every sentence on the deck as well. When a rule changes in `references/rules.md`, its test changes here in the same edit (and the other way round).

## Before the first slide

- The deck is cloned from an existing course deck, and archetypes are duplicated with `add_slide.py`, not rebuilt. (The house system)

## On every slide

- Calibri throughout; colors from the house palette: teal `0D9488` eyebrows, badges, closing line; deep blue `0A5A8A` row labels, column heads; slate `2D3B45` headline, body; grey `6B7780` slide number, footnotes; `E8F1F8` text on dark slides. (The house system)
- A content slide carries its caps eyebrow top left and course · slide number top right. (The house system)
- The headline is a claim, not a label, and repeats nothing the slide's own furniture already states. (The house system; One point per slide)
- One point on the slide, rarely two. (One point per slide)
- A repeated sequence's payoff sits alone on the next slide, not on the last item; a break is a one-word slide. (One point per slide)
- No slide only asserts a belief: the claim is folded into the slide that motivates it, and the why comes before the activity it justifies. (Fold a claim into the slide that earns it)
- A step that uses an interactive tool is that tool's slide, not a description of it; a Pear Deck slide is left plain with the right title and instruction, and the handover says he applies the add-on. (Interactive slides)
- "We", not "you", where the difficulty is shared; his own stake is in first person. (Register)
- A set of distinct parallel facts is label-first bullets; prose bullets only for one idea developing. (Register)
- No sentence names a worry and then soothes it. Alan keeps adding these. (Register)
- Timings are ranges ("5-10 minutes"). (Register)
- No bullet is a noun phrase plus an em-dash gloss (the no-telegrams rule). (Building a session deck)
- Where a skill is coming, the slide points forward to it; an activity's question is sharpened toward the skill being built. (Register)

## The closing slide

- It is titled Reminders, not "This week", and carries: the graded item with its due date; OYP items do not affect the final grade except as a substitute for something missed; graded items carry a 10% late penalty, no exceptions; the next session's shape; where to ask questions. (The closing slide is Reminders)

## Before it reaches him

- The whole deck has been run against `writing-to-teach`. (Checklist)
